  "title": "Government-Wide Research Hub",
  "question": "How can all saved government research, entity relationships, committee records, adjudicated movements and exact evidence gaps be explored in one governed hub without flattening institutions or replacing each package's evidence ownership?",
  "bluf": "The Government-Wide Research Hub brings every exact Catalog package card and the complete Registry shelf into the same navigable destination as the 642-node Federal Group chart, 401 governed attachment associations, 29 congressional bodies with exact committee-corpus artifacts, eight adjudicated movements and a typed gap board. Each package now opens as a wide reading room with curated routes, complete files and a package-scoped entity map that visibly separates exact joins from review-only Catalog mentions. Package browsing, attachment, coverage, movement and incompleteness remain separate evidence layers.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-09-22T11:51:46-04:00",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "The authored movement registry contains eight adjudicated records through the stated research cutoff. Exact research attachments, complete Registry membership and typed gap projections are regenerated from their current named owners, with source hashes recorded at build time. Catalog entity labels remain review-only candidates. This is neither a live government-state feed, a second return queue nor the Government-Wide Source Monitor inbox.",
  "use_note": "Use as the one browsing hub for saved government research, every registered file, the entity chart, committees, adjudicated movement and typed next checks. Reconcile already-completed research and exact custody before launching new searches. Follow every package, movement or gap to its controlling owner before citing facts. Catalog entity mentions are searchable but do not create chart attachments. Do not infer legal ownership from tree containment, admit raw monitor candidates, or treat Catalog registration as authorization for Chronicle promotion, a watch, Federal Group mutation, app/site shipment, commit or push.",
